================================================================================
env.summary - Stage7 environment variables by consuming service
================================================================================

Generated from the current source tree. Every entry below is read via
process.env in non-test service source (services/*/src, shared-nextgen/src,
frontend-nextgen/src). Regenerated alongside the .env.example cleanup.

Scope notes
-----------
* docker-compose.yaml mounts the whole .env into every container through
  "env_file". The sections here describe what each service READS, not what it
  receives. A variable can therefore be visible to a service it does not use.
* Values shown are the .env.example defaults or placeholders. Never put a real
  secret in this file; it is committed.
* .env is read by Docker Compose at build time too. worker-pool takes
  STAGE7_ASSISTANTS as a build arg and prunes unselected assistant folders from
  the image, so changing it requires a rebuild of that image.
* NODE_ENV and NODE_OPTIONS are not read by application code, but they are
  consumed by the Node runtime and the frontend build, so they still have an
  effect. They stay in .env.example for that reason.
* STORAGE_DIR and SAFE_VALUE appear only in test fixtures (probe-executor
  tests) and are deliberately absent from .env.example.

Variables read by code that .env.example omits
-----------------------------------------------
None. The template now covers every process.env read in non-test source.
Two are documented comment-only because they must not be set in .env:
PATH (read by CodeExecutor for subprocess environments) and PORT (each
service's default is its documented port; overrides are set per container in
docker-compose.yaml). AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY are documented
as fallbacks in the ARTIFACTS_S3_* comments.

Formerly documented variables that no longer exist anywhere in the code
------------------------------------------------------------------------
PLANNER_MAX_ATTEMPTS, PLANNER_MAX_TRANSPORT_ATTEMPTS (planner controls were
removed), GEMINI_API_URL and ANTHROPIC_MESSAGES_PATH (Gemini and Anthropic
endpoints are hardcoded in their provider classes), OLLAMA_PROXY_BASE, and the
legacy v6 variables: CLIENT_SECRET, SHARED_SECRET, ADMIN_SECRET,
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET, GITHUB_TOKEN, GITHUB_USERNAME, GIT_REPOSITORY_URL,
GIT_DEFAULT_BRANCH, GITHUB_EMAIL, POSTOFFICE_URL, LIBRARIAN_URL, and all
per-service *_SECRET values. Also removed from the summary: SMTP_* (no longer
read by any executor), TEMPORAL_ADDRESS, TEMPORAL_OP_TIMEOUT_MS, and
TEMPORAL_GET_RESULT_TIMEOUT_MS (temporal now reads TEMPORAL_HTTP_URL,
TEMPORAL_TASK_QUEUE, APPROVAL_*, and WATCH_SCHEDULER_POLL_MS instead).

================================================================================
/infrastructure - mongo, redis (docker-compose.yaml)
================================================================================

Neither container has an env_file, and neither service reads process.env.
They are configured entirely in docker-compose.yaml.

No environment variables.

================================================================================
/shared-nextgen
================================================================================

SERVICE_NAME=stage7
  Log source label for the shared pino logger.

================================================================================
/services/gateway  (host 3900, container 3000)
================================================================================

PORT=3000
  Container listen port. Default: 3000.

WORKER_POOL_URL=http://worker-pool:3200
  Backend used by the /api/workers routes. Default: http://worker-pool:3200.

SERVICE_NAME=stage7
  Via shared-nextgen logger.

GATEWAY_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=300
  Requests per minute the proxy allows per client IP before responding 429.
  Default: 300.

Gateway routes for the other services use hard-coded container URLs
(brain:3100, worker-pool:3200, agent-runtime:3400,
tool-executor:3500, temporal:4100, vault:4000, artifacts:4200,
auth:4300). Those are not configurable through the environment; change them
in services/gateway/src/index.ts.

================================================================================
/services/brain  (host 3100, container 3100)
================================================================================

PORT=3100

-- Connection ------------------------------------------------------------------

REDIS_HOST=redis
REDIS_PORT=6379
  Semantic cache backend.

ARTIFACTS_URL=http://artifacts:4200
PERSISTENCE_URL=
  Persistence for skill collections. ARTIFACTS_URL is used first;
  PERSISTENCE_URL is a legacy alias fallback. Default:
  http://artifacts:4200.

-- LLM providers ---------------------------------------------------------------

brain registers a provider only when its credential is present, so an unset
key means that provider is absent from the router rather than failing calls.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_BASE=https://api.openai.com/v1
OPENAI_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
OPENAI_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
OPENAI_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

GROK_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=
  Either key enables the Grok provider.
GROK_API_BASE=https://api.x.ai/v1
GROK_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
GROK_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
GROK_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

MISTRAL_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_BASE=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
MISTRAL_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
MISTRAL_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
MISTRAL_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

GEMINI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
  Either key enables Gemini. The endpoint is hardcoded to
  https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com in the provider; there is no
  URL variable.

HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=
HF_TOKEN=
  Either credential enables Hugging Face.
HUGGINGFACE_API_BASE=https://router.huggingface.co/v1
HUGGINGFACE_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
HUGGINGFACE_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
HUGGINGFACE_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
OPENROUTER_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
OPENROUTER_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
OPENROUTER_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

NVIDIA_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_BASE=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
NVIDIA_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
NVIDIA_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
NVIDIA_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
  Endpoint is hardcoded to https://api.anthropic.com in the provider.

OPENWEB_URL=
OPENWEBUI_URL=
  Either base URL enables the OpenWebUI provider. A trailing /v1 is stripped.
OPENWEBUI_API_KEY=
OPENWEB_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/api/models
OPENWEB_CHAT_PATH=/api/chat/completions
OPENWEB_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/api/completions
OPENWEBUI_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
OPENWEBUI_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
OPENWEBUI_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions
  The OPENWEB_* path variables are checked first, then the OPENWEBUI_* ones.

OLLAMA_API_BASE=http://localhost:11434/v1
OLLAMA_URL=
  Either base enables Ollama; a missing /v1 suffix is appended.
OLLAMA_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_LIST_MODELS_PATH=/models
OLLAMA_CHAT_PATH=/chat/completions
OLLAMA_COMPLETIONS_PATH=/completions

CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_ACCOUNT_ID=

CUSTOM_PROVIDERS=
  Comma-separated third-party provider prefixes, e.g. REQUESTY,LLM7. Each
  prefix P requires P_API_KEY, P_API_NAME, and P_API_URL to be OpenAI
  compatible, and may set P_LIST_MODELS_PATH. Read dynamically as
  process.env[`${prefix}_...`] in customProviders.ts. Example set:
  REQUESTY_API_KEY, REQUESTY_API_NAME, REQUESTY_API_URL.

-- Timeouts and circuit breaker ------------------------------------------------

BRAIN_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
BRAIN_PROVIDER_ATTEMPT_TIMEOUT_MS=660000
BRAIN_COMPLETION_DEADLINE_MS=1800000
BRAIN_CIRCUIT_THRESHOLD=8
BRAIN_CIRCUIT_COOLDOWN_MS=60000
BRAIN_MODEL_COOLDOWN_MAX_MS=86400000
  Ceiling on how long a model stays in cooldown after a failure (ms).

================================================================================
/services/worker-pool  (host 3200, container 3200)
================================================================================

PORT=3200

STAGE7_ASSISTANTS=
  Comma-separated assistant IDs to load. Empty means all 21. Also passed as
  the image build arg, which prunes the other assistant folders out of the
  image. An unknown ID fails the build (image) or refuses to boot (runtime).
  Valid IDs are the folder names under services/worker-pool/assistants/:
  analytics, career, content, cto, education, event, executive, finance,
  healthcare, hotel, hr, investment, legal, marketing, product, restaurant,
  sales, scriptwriter, songwriter, sports, support. The -canonical-assistant
  suffix is accepted and stripped.

REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379
  Task queue and cache.

MONGO_URI=mongodb://mongo:27017
MONGO_DB=stage7
  Read indirectly: worker-pool builds its persistence layer from
  ArtifactsService, which is the artifacts workspace library
  (@stage7-nextgen/artifacts). When MONGO_URI is set but Mongo is
  unreachable, this service refuses to start instead of falling back to a
  volatile in-memory store, and logs that MONGO_URI is not set when it is
  absent.

BRAIN_URL=http://brain:3100
TOOL_EXECUTOR_URL=http://tool-executor:3500
  Downstream services used by assistant runtimes.

================================================================================
/services/mcp-runtime  (host 3300, container 3300)
/services/agent-runtime  (host 3400, container 3400)
================================================================================

PORT=3400

TOOL_EXECUTOR_URL=http://tool-executor:3500
  Downstream base for tool execution. Default: http://tool-executor:3500.

================================================================================
/services/tool-executor  (host 3500, container 3500)
================================================================================

PORT=3500

-- Downstream services ---------------------------------------------------------

ARTIFACTS_URL=http://artifacts:4200
BRAIN_URL=http://brain:3100
WORKER_POOL_URL=http://worker-pool:3200
  Downstream bases for skills and reasoning delegation. BRAIN_URL must stay
  set: a skill that falls back to a direct brain call skips the call entirely
  when it is empty.

PERSISTENCE_URL=
AGENT_RUNTIME_URL=http://agent-runtime:3400
  Also read as base-origin candidates for outbound HTTP: after a skill URL
  fails, tool-executor retries the same path against each of ARTIFACTS_URL,
  PERSISTENCE_URL, BRAIN_URL, WORKER_POOL_URL, and AGENT_RUNTIME_URL in turn
  before giving up.

TEMPORAL_HTTP_URL=http://temporal:4100
  Used by the shared Temporal instance for workflow operations.

VAULT_URL=http://vault:4000
  Secret decryption endpoint used by the credential provider and CodeExecutor.

TOOL_EXECUTOR_SERVICE_ID=
  tool-executor's service identity for minting a bearer token from the auth
  service (POST /api/auth/service/auth). Required for vault access: the vault
  authenticates calls by verified service token and derives tenant identity
  from it. Register the account with POST /api/auth/services.

TOOL_EXECUTOR_SERVICE_API_KEY=
  The API key paired with TOOL_EXECUTOR_SERVICE_ID when minting vault service
  tokens.

MCP_RUNTIME_URL=http://mcp-runtime:3300/mcp
  Default MCP discovery source for the library source registry.

-- Assistant persistence homes -------------------------------------------------

ASSISTANT_HOME=
  Shared assistant storage path used by skills and CodeExecutor. A skill that
  declares persistenceEnvVar with no matching variable falls back to the
  shared assistant storage. Default: /tmp/stage7 (or /var/data/stage7/<name>
  per skill).

-- Stores and local paths ------------------------------------------------------

SKILL_STORE_DIR=
SKILL_STORE_TIMEOUT_MS=3000
  Skill-record store; local dir defaults to /tmp/stage7-store, remote
  (Mongo-backed) calls time out at SKILL_STORE_TIMEOUT_MS.

TOOL_STORE_DIR=
  Tool-record store. Default: the service's built-in store directory.

TRIGGER_STORE_DIR=
TRIGGER_STORE_TIMEOUT_MS=3000
  Trigger-record store. Default: /tmp/stage7-triggers.

EXECUTION_RECORD_DIR=
EXECUTION_RECORD_TIMEOUT_MS=3000
  Execution-record store. Default: /tmp/stage7-executions.

EVENT_LOG_DIR=
EVENT_LOG_TIMEOUT_MS=3000
  Event log. Default: /tmp/stage7-events.

TOOL_AUDIT_LOG_DIR=
  Tool audit log. Default: /tmp/stage7-tool-audit.

TOOL_GRANT_STORE_DIR=
TOOL_DENIAL_STORE_DIR=
  Tool grant/denial stores. Default: /tmp/stage7-tool-grants.

TOOL_PERMISSION_REQUEST_STORE_DIR=
  Pending tool-permission requests. Default: /tmp/stage7-tool-permissions.

MCP_CONFIG_PATH=
  MCP server config file for the mcpServers routes.
  Default: /tmp/stage7-mcp/mcp-servers.json.

MCP_DISCOVERY_SOURCES=
  JSON array overriding MCP discovery sources; merged with the
  MCP_RUNTIME_URL default.

PLUGIN_DEPLOY_DIR=
  Compiled plugin deploy target. Default: /tmp/stage7-plugins.

STAGE7_SANDBOX_DIR=
  Sandbox root for skill code execution. Empty means platform default.

STAGE7_PROBE_WORK_DIR=
  Working directory for probe execution and harness edits.
  Default: process.cwd().

PYTHON_BIN=python3
  Python interpreter for code and plugin generation.

FILE_STORAGE_BASE_PATH=
  File storage executor root. Default: /tmp/stage7-filestore.

CALENDAR_BASE_PATH=
  Calendar executor root. Default: /tmp/stage7-calendars.

API_CLIENT_BASE_URL=
  Default base URL for the ApiClient executor when a skill does not provide
  one (a skill credential api_base_url wins).

TOOL_DISCOVERY_NETWORK=false
  Set to the literal string "true" to let tool discovery probe containerized
  tools on the Docker network. Anything else, including unset, keeps discovery
  local.

PATH=
  Read by CodeExecutor when building subprocess environments. Not set via
  .env; listed for completeness.

-- Search and scraping ---------------------------------------------------------

SEARXNG_URL=
  External SearXNG instance. Not part of this compose file. A skill-level
  searxng_url credential wins when present.

GOOGLE_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_SEARCH_ENGINE_ID=
  Google Programmable Search credentials.

LANGSEARCH_API_KEY=
LANGSEARCH_API_URL=https://api.langsearch.com

-- Tenant policy ---------------------------------------------------------------

HARNESS_LEARNING_TENANTS=
  Optional comma-separated allowlist of tenant IDs permitted to use harness
  learning. Empty means all tenants are allowed.

LOG_LEVEL=info

